{
  "name": "Vesper Staff",
  "type": "weapon",
  "img": "icons/weapons/staves/staff-simple-gold.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>A staff of black ash capped with a lens of smoked glass. Held up to a light, the lens does not darken the light — it darkens the eye that looks through it.</em></p><p><strong>Staff, very rare (requires attunement by a Cleric, Sorcerer, or Wizard)</strong></p><p>This staff can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff. You gain a <strong>+2 bonus</strong> to attack rolls and damage rolls made with it. While holding it, you also gain a <strong>+2 bonus</strong> to spell attack rolls and to the saving throw DCs of your spells.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> The staff has <strong>10 charges</strong> and regains <strong>1d6 + 4</strong> expended charges daily at dawn. While holding it, you can expend charges to cast one of the following spells from it, using your spell save DC: <em>Darkness</em> (2 charges), <em>Invisibility</em> (2 charges), <em>Dispel Magic</em> (3 charges), or <em>Counterspell</em> (3 charges).</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
